Room A
Room A. There is a counter here. Room B is to the east.
You can see a counter (on which are an apple, a rope, a map, a bell and a lamp) and a shopkeeper here.
> prices
The shopkeeper is happy.
The apple costs 5 coins (cheap).
The rope costs 20 coins (fair).
The map costs 45 coins (dear).
The bell costs 10 coins (fair).
The lamp costs 15 coins (fair).
5 things on the counter.
> buy apple
You buy the apple for 5 coins.
> take rope
You have to buy it first.
> haggle rope
The shopkeeper smiles. The rope costs 16 coins (fair).
> buy rope
You buy the rope for 21 coins.
> smile
The shopkeeper smiles back.
> buy lamp
You buy the lamp for 15 coins.
> buy bell
You can't afford that. The bell costs 10 coins (fair).
> sell apple
You sell the apple for 2 coins.
> buy bell
You buy the bell for 10 coins.
> buy apple
You can't afford that. The apple costs 5 coins (cheap).
> receipt
1. rope: 21
2. lamp: 15
3. bell: 10
Total: 46 coins
Dearest: 21.
The shopkeeper falls asleep.
> bag
In your bag: bell, lamp and rope.
Room for 1 more.
(THE LAMP IS ON THE RECEIPT)
> purse
You have 1 coin. You spent 51 coins and got back 2 coins.
> tally
0 fives and 1 left over.
[]
> turn on lamp
The lamp is lit. It will burn for 3 turns.
> haggle bell
The shopkeeper won't haggle again.
> sell map
You don't have that.
> inventory
You're carrying:
  a bell
  a lamp (providing light)
  a rope
The lamp goes out.
> east
Room B
Room B. It is dark in the corner. Room A is to the west.
